From d5b0108374c6601622ddeda3c99c201d7b532014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 5317: an empty enrichment queue is looked at by one worker,
 not four
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ops, 16 Oct 01:05Z: around the nightly enrichment run the queue's claim
waited 11.8 s for one of the background pool's two connections, four
claims at a time, with nothing queued — every five seconds, competing
with the nightly run for the same two connections.

While the last claim found nothing, the ticker starts one worker; the
full four start once a claim finds a job or a contact is queued.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
